    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2601.21905v1</id>
    <title>A priori bounds for some infinitely renormalizable quadratic: IV. Elephant Eyes</title>
    <updated>2026-01-29T16:00:14Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.21905v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2601.21905v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>In this paper we prove a priori bounds for an ``elephant eye'' combinatorics. Little $M$-copies specifying these combinatorics are allowed to converge to the cusp of the Mandelbrot set. To handle it, we develope a new geometric tool: uniform thin-thick decompositions for bordered Riemann surfaces.</summary>
